          "id": "http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416",
          "type": "Type",
          "_label": "Details (Official List Description)"
        }
      ],
      "content": "GREAT GADDESDEN        GADDESDEN ROW TL 01 SW                                         (South side)                                         Jockey End 3/87                                    Plough Cottages -                                       Nos. 1, 2, and 3 -                                       II 2 houses, now 3. Lower E part C16 or early C17, W part C18, brick fronts C19, brick gables C20. Timber frame now exposed only on 1st floor rear of E part, otherwise roughcast, red brick front and end walls, steep old red tile roofs. A long irregular 2-storeys range, facing N, at corner with Bradden Lane. 3 windows on each floor to each part. Flush 3-light casement windows with small panes and segmental arches on ground floor. 2 low plank doors to E part date from when it was 3 cottages Similar door to adjoining W part and gabled porch further to W. Older E part has 3-bays structure with clasped-purlin roof and chamfered axial floor beams. Listing NGR: TL0395513679"
    }
  ],
